# =============================================================================
# OIST coral tank ITS2 eDNA analysis, v3
#
# What changed from OIST_Tank_analysis_revised.R, and why:
#   1. Heat and Flow are coded -0.5/+0.5, so every Heat/Flow row in every model
#      is a true main effect (the old treatment coding gave simple effects).
#   2. PERMANOVA now tests Heat and Flow main effects (additive model, margin)
#      plus the interaction. The old file only reported Heat:Flow.
#   3. A tank-label permutation test uses ALL samples and ALL dates. It
#      compares between-treatment and within-treatment tank dissimilarity
#      within each date, so date-wide shocks cancel out.
#   4. Drift excludes each tank's first sample (it is 0 by construction) and
#      uses days since that tank's own first sample.
#   5. Turnover is modelled against log(gap days); distances saturate.
#   6. Distance-to-control is replaced by a full same-date tank-pair table,
#      with control-vs-control as the baseline.
#   7. Host similarity gets a permutation null, own-tank rank, a
#      "no generalist sequences" version, a presence/absence version, and a
#      species-level reference.
#   8. Sequence status uses prevalence thresholds (8534_A is no longer
#      "detected in both" because of one host sample).
#   9. Three scenarios rerun the core tests: all data, rare-sequence tail
#      removed, and a core period without sparse dates or the long late gap.
#  10. SIMPER p-values are gone. Sequence-level tests use tank means.
#  11. Inlet QC, an other-date inlet null, and an other-tank host null for the
#      overlap fractions.
#  12. Every model effect goes into one table with CI and an approximate
#      minimum detectable effect, so you can say what the design could detect.
#
# Terminology: the abundance tables are post-MED ITS2 sequences, not SymPortal
# type profiles. This script calls them "sequences" throughout.
# =============================================================================

